// The browser UI: the playground application (src/playground/app/) and the
// four docs/ pages' scripts (src/site/). Both touch `document`, `window`,
// `localStorage` and the DOM event model, none of which exist in the engine's
// ES2023-plus-Node world.
//
// They get their own program rather than DOM being added to
// tsconfig.base.json, so that the engine and the CLI keep failing the
// typecheck if they ever reach for a browser global — the property that made
// the node:fs port (src/fs/reader.ts) worth building in the first place.
//
// One program for both, not two: they share the CDN-library declarations
// (`marked` is used by five pages and declared once), and a second config
// would buy separation between two directories that are the same kind of
// thing.
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2023", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"]
  },
  "include": ["src/playground/app", "src/site", "test/playground/app", "test/site"]
}
